NNAAMMEE
     rrwwhhoo — who is logged in on local machines

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rrwwhhoo [--aa]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rrwwhhoo command produces output similar to who(1), but for all machines
     on the local network.  If no report has been received from a machine for
     11 minutes then rrwwhhoo assumes the machine is down, and does not report
     users last known to be logged into that machine.

     If a user has not typed to the system for a minute or more, then rrwwhhoo re‐
     ports this idle time.

     The following option is available:

     --aa      Include all users.  By default, if a user has not typed to the
             system for an hour or more, then the user will be omitted from
             the output.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/rwho/whod.*  information about other machines

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ruptime(1), who(1), rwhod(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The rrwwhhoo command appeared in 4.3BSD.

BBUUGGSS
     This is unwieldy when the number of machines on the local net is large.

